package skill

// Endpoint activity and complete-pair residence answer different questions.
// Share the callable entry and measurement boundaries, not a fixed workflow.
const TraceIOActivityTeaching = "For IO event rates, byte rates, read/write proportions or size distributions use view=\"window_stats\", section io_activity (not a new view). It counts independently admitted endpoint events, including unpaired endpoints; io_inflight occupancy and request latency require complete pairs. Keep source/layer/endpoint family/phase/device/byte caliber separate: observed event counts are not unique request counts, and RQ/BIO/filesystem layers must not be added as independent work. Read direction and known-byte denominators, missing-size counts and coverage before comparing proportions. Rates divide by the full selected time window; bucket_ms selects time buckets, including idle buckets and the actual short-tail width. Explicit positive-width windows are half-open; an automatically selected capture endpoint is included only as disclosed by end_inclusive. Line bounds take precedence; line-only and point selections have no rate denominator. Missing rates or sizes are unavailable, not zero; known zero is valid. Request size alone does not prove random/sequential access. Use published group/window values and omissions, not displayed witnesses or paired-request counts, to describe IO活动次数、读写比例、字节速率、大小分布. These measurements are workload context, not target blocking time or root-cause evidence."
